August 4th 2026- Got more clarity on what exactly SAR and inSAR do. inSAR  has no part to play in my thesis project simply because it fails to have any impact or figure out how exactly forest data works at all. InSAR for forests is not "difficult" or "noisy" — it is non-functional, inSAR works only on hard stable surfaces but fails to work when it comes to cases like these.
However, SAR has a part to play because it can parse monsoon clouds and is needed for basic monitoring of whether the site has any forest growing or not. The issue in case of SAR however is that it fails to distinguish between forests and plantations at all. It can help out for basic monitoring however, as i mentioned as it can help in noticing the presence of any sort of clearing out of forest surfaces etc.
